  "dom_id": "step-q129453",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=4 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-2)=2\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{2}=2+2=4.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=4$ and ${x}_{3}=-2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-4-(-2)=4\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{1}=4+4-2=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=6$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=-2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $\u27e86,4,-2\u27e9.$",
